[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

Off-grid electricity for [b]Build 42[/b]: solar, wind, pedal, water, steam and gas, stored in battery banks and run from a charge controller. Light your base after the shutoff and wire whole houses back up.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core 1.9.0 or newer[/b] (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Built for it, not yet tested on a dedicated server[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes. Saves from Off-Grid: Solar Power do not carry over[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-first.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/first-system.png?v=2[/img]
[olist]
[*]Place a [b]solar array[/b] in the open, facing the sun.
[*]Place a [b]battery bank[/b] and load it with car batteries.
[*]Place a [b]charge controller[/b].
[*]Run a cable from each part to the controller (right-click, Connect), then switch it on.
[/olist]
The in-game [b]Dazed Mod Suite Guide[/b] (the book button on the left sidebar) walks through the rest.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-make.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/sources.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Solar arrays[/b], [b]tracking arrays[/b] that follow the sun (up to 15% more), and a 2x2 [b]Large Solar Array[/b]. Snow, dust and wear cut output.
[*][b]Windmills[/b] that turn to follow the wind, plus a windsock and weather vane to read it.
[*][b]Pedal generators[/b] you sit on and ride.
[*]A [b]micro-hydro wheel[/b] beside water: a steady 350 W, slower in ice.
[*][b]Steam engines[/b] burn fuel and drink water.
[*][b]Propane, petrol and wood gas generators[/b] start and stop on their own at the levels you set. Makeshift ones are pull-start. Wood gas burns logs and planks, warms up for a few minutes and needs its ash cleaned out.
[*][b]Car alternator[/b]: a parked car with its engine running feeds up to 500 W.
[*][b]Treadmill generator[/b]: wire a gym treadmill to a controller and walk, run or sprint on it. Fitness 0 to 10 makes 50 to 150 W walking, double running, 3.5 times sprinting; sprinting tires you.
[*][b]Zombie treadwheel[/b]: knock a zombie down, tie it with a rope (you see the rope), lead it home and put it in the wheel, where the real zombie walks for ever: about 80 W, 140 W while someone stands close. Running on a taut rope can snap it.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-store.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/storage.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Battery banks[/b]: floor racks hold 3, 6 or 8 car batteries, wall boxes 2, 3 or 4. Cold lowers capacity, cycles wear cells, and a low-voltage disconnect protects them.
[*][b]Charge controllers[/b]: Makeshift manages 8 parts, Workshop 24.
[*][b]Load priority[/b]: Essential, Normal or Low per machine. As the batteries run down, Low is cut first.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/board.png?v=2[/img]
Right-click the controller, [b]System monitor[/b]: the analog charge board shows sources and load on two dials, how long the bank lasts at this draw, every cell, today's harvest, every circuit, the main isolator and your generators.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-gear.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/gear.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Transformers[/b] carry power across town and wire whole buildings through Dazed Core's [b]Building Picker[/b]: lights and appliances inside work off your batteries.
[*][b]Charger bench[/b] for loose batteries; any wired part charges a parked car within 10 tiles.
[*][b]Electric fence[/b] stuns zombies, never people. [b]Room cooler[/b] keeps a whole room's food like a fridge. [b]Space heater[/b] warms its room with Dazed Climate.
[*][b]Wall gauge[/b], [b]solar lamps[/b], and the [b]Knox County Almanac[/b]: read the sky for a month of weather.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-hazard.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/hazards.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Wiring a live system can burn your hand. Switch the controller off first.
[*]Thunderstorms can trip the isolator or damage the controller. A [b]grounding rod[/b] near the controller takes the strike.
[*]A Makeshift bank charged hard in a closed room builds up hydrogen. Open a window.
[*]A generator under a roof fills the building with fumes. Run it outside.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-tiers.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/tiers.png?v=2[/img]
Most parts come as [b]Makeshift[/b], [b]Salvaged[/b] or [b]Workshop[/b]. Learn them from the [i]Dazed Power Handbook[/i] and [i]Workshop Power Systems[/i], or find solar rigs on houses around Knox County. Electricians know every Makeshift build. Anything over 30 kg is carried as parts.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-works.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Dazed Plumbing[/b]: generators and steam engines feed from piped tanks; pumps, purifier, fuel pump and drilled well run off your controller.
[*][b]Dazed Climate[/b]: heater and cooler change room temperature; batteries and engines feel the cold.
[*][b]Dazed Cooking[/b]: the food dehydrator runs off your system.
[*][b]Dazed Essentials[/b]: bulk jobs leave powered machines alone.
[*][b]Electric Vehicles[/b]: charge homemade EVs from your banks.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-sandbox.png?v=2[/img]
18 options, from array output and battery wear to lightning, cable cost, found solar gear and the treadwheel. Or pick one [b]preset[/b] (Easy, Standard, Realistic, Hardcore) on the Dazed Core page to set them all at once.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-compat.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Do not run it alongside Off-Grid: Solar Power; Dazed Power replaces it.
[*][b]Dazed Dank[/b] (0.57+, Core 1.8.4+): grow lights, fans, heaters, ACs, humidifiers, pumps and the drying fan cabled to a controller or transformer are Power loads: billed on the LOADS page, in Load Priority (Grow lights, Fans, Hydro pumps, Grow climate), dark when cut, no controller slot. Uncabled gear still runs free off a lit square.
[*]If something desyncs in multiplayer, please tell me.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Power/images/h-help.png?v=2[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab or open an issue on [url=https://github.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPower]GitHub[/url]. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

